lines += ['','### One exception remains open','','V1 p962, main CP 1076183–1076184, contains the single source codepoint U+F079. Both enlarged views show the ornate stacked honorific, and the original embedded AGA Arabesque font confirms glyph92 with 14 contours. Its lexical reading is رضي الله عنهم. The PDF font does not separately encode every interior diacritic, and this review does not establish a complete vocalized Unicode expansion. The correct result is to preserve the original codepoint, leave the visible transcription null, and retain `p07-1-929-v01-p0962-r05-chars-unresolved`. This retained source limitation is not a newly introduced defect.','','### Appendix and cover evidence is source-faithful','','All 220 tail character regions were compared with the 13 full-page views and their raw source spans. The covered source intervals have no missing codepoints: V1 main [6771,6837), V2 main [0,605), and V2 main [951605,959535).','','The appendix has 53 rows including its header and 52 numbered entries. The independently read printed-number sequence matches the bridge file. Each row has three visible content columns and a fourth empty DOC row-terminator slot. All 212 cell slots were checked against exact source slices and terminators. Entries continued across page boundaries remain joined to their original row.','','The critic cells for printed references **917, 954, 1649, 1731 and 1765** are empty in the original. There are five source cells but seven page-level blank regions because 954 and 1731 span pages. No critic name is supplied.','','The source anomalies are visible and correctly preserved: the ampersand after entry794; the incomplete critic label beginning only র ইবনু হাওশাব; repeated করে করে in entry801; literal less-than signs in entries894,896 and1495; and এতটি in entry1498. The cover metadata and image logos are distinguished from report body text.','','The appendix’s weak-grade heading, critic labels and quoted excerpts remain edition claims. This review does not independently grade hadith, authenticate chains, identify every narrator, establish canonical numbering, or certify an excerpt as complete matn.','','## Structural corroboration','','The independent checks passed '+str(struct['check_count']+follow['check_count'])+' assertions with zero unresolved assertion failures. Material checks include:','','- 28 original-PDF rerenders matched author evidence pixel for pixel.','- All 14 review and 14 region correction before-states matched the authenticated parent exactly.','- Every declared exact source slice matched the parent raw story export.','- The 13 resolution events reference existing parent exceptions; the remaining honorific exception is retained.','- The selected original glyph draws and extracted font bytes/outlines match the supplied evidence.','- Bengali p641 uses the actual F2 resource and the embedded GSUB rules independently corroborate the extra ra-phala.','- Every completed after-transcription can be derived from unchanged source plus exact inherited display mappings; existing difference records are preserved.','- All 156 parent semantic evidence links and 19 new tail semantic spans match exact source/parent records.','','The source-derived transcriptions for large inherited regions were checked mechanically. Only their localized target crops were independently reread here; the remainder of those pages retains its previous review provenance.','','## Page observation ledger','','The full machine-readable per-page observations, exact CP spans, region IDs and image hashes are in `page_observations.jsonl`; the appendix row/cell observations are in `appendix_row_observations.jsonl`. The following notes record what the complete-page readings established:','']
